    "summary": "Three study drawings of a hyena; single-page drawing on an album folio. Two profiled hyenas face the opposite direction (drawn in full), while the third and central drawing depicts a detailed face. Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
